import json
d = json.load(open("/workspace/train/calcs/tender_weight_study.json"))
o = []; p = o.append
p("# PF-CT R2 Tender — Weight-reduction study TW-1")
p("Pulsipher Farms Christmas Train — preliminary, not for construction until PE stamped. Study note TW-1, 27 Oct 2026. Basis: rev T1 tender (owner plan LT45.1), CAD mass report, owner tender ledger (Project Plan Page), tender-lt45/basis.json. Masses are screening estimates; ASSUMED items are marked. No supplier data is invented.")
p("## 1. Answer in plain words")
p(f"- Yes. Built up honestly, the tender as drawn is about {d['baseline_kg']:,.0f} kg, not 8,160 kg: the trucks are lighter than the ledger allowed, but the 6 mm skin, PL10 deck, deck outriggers and the 3 mm coal cover are heavier. At that mass the 2% start margin at 350 bar is only {d['margin']['baseline']:.2f} kN.")
p(f"- A package of seven low-labor changes saves about {d['save_kg']:,} kg and gets the tender to about {d['new_kg']:,} kg ({d['new_noG_kg']:,} kg if the lighter generator does not happen). That is at or below the 8,160 kg ledger and {d['limit_t']-d['new_noG_kg']/1000:.1f}–{d['limit_t']-d['new_kg']/1000:.1f} t under the ≈{d['limit_t']:.1f} t limit where 400 bar would be needed.")
p(f"- New 2% start margin at 350 bar: {d['margin']['package']:.2f} kN (package) / {d['margin']['package_noG']:.2f} kN (without the genset saving), against {d['margin']['ledger_8160']:.2f} kN at the 8,160 kg ledger and {d['margin']['baseline']:.2f} kN as drawn.")
p("- Top moves: (1) 10 ga steel skin on posts instead of 6 mm plate; (2) 6 mm tread-plate deck on cross-bearers instead of PL10 + outriggers; (3) an open-skid 35 kW genset, because the insulated tender already is the sound enclosure; (4) lighter coal cover, fish-belly bolsters and lighter lining. The look stays: black with gold trim, the coal-effect cover stays, and the bolted skin reads as riveted tender plate.")
p("- Moving equipment to the locomotive does not help the 2% start: the train weighs the same and the motors, not adhesion, are the limit. " + d["ballast_note"])
p("## 2. Mass breakdown (rev T1 tender, as drawn, built up)")
p(f"- Wheel modeling fix: the CAD models each Ø600 wheel as a solid disc ({d['wheel_cad_kg']:.0f} kg). A plate-web wheel (rim 50 deep, web 25, hub Ø200, ASSUMED section) is ≈ {d['wheel_true_kg']:.0f} kg. Eight wheels: {8*d['wheel_cad_kg']:,.0f} → {8*d['wheel_true_kg']:,.0f} kg. The same overstatement exists on the coach and loco CAD wheels (CAD mass only; the ledgers are not affected).")
p("| Group | Item | kg | Basis |"); p("|---|---|---|---|")
for g, items in d["ledger"].items():
    for i in items: p(f"| {g} | {i['item']} | {i['kg']:,.0f} | {i['basis']} |")
p(""); p("| Group | kg |"); p("|---|---|")
for g, v in d["groups"].items(): p(f"| {g} | {v:,.0f} |")
p(f"| Total | {d['baseline_kg']:,.0f} |")
p("- Against the owner's ledger (8,160 kg): trucks 2,643 vs 4,000 allowed (lighter); frame + body 4,403 vs 2,141 allowed (much heavier); equipment and fluids about 2,270 vs 2,019 (mounts/exhaust allowance added).")
p("## 3. Candidate savings")
p("| ID | Move | kg saved | Shop h | Eng h | Approvability | Look | Recommended |"); p("|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for c in d["candidates"]:
    p(f"| {c['id']} | {c['move']} | {c['kg']:,} | {c['shop_h']:+d} | {c['eng_h']:+d} | {c['approv']} | {c['look']} | {'YES' if c['rec'] else 'no'} |")
p("## 4. Recommended package")
for c in d["candidates"]:
    if c["rec"]: p(f"- {c['id']}: {c['move']} — {c['kg']:,} kg")
p(f"- Total {d['save_kg']:,} kg → tender ≈ {d['new_kg']:,} kg ({d['new_noG_kg']:,} kg without G1). Labor: about +38 shop h and +22 engineering h in total; all steel work CWF already does (plate, forming, CNC cutting).")
p("- Not touched: main rails HSS10x4x1/4, crossmembers at the ends, PF-DB drop boxes and pockets. So the 200 kN buff check (C5, C5w) and the fatigue details at the coupler are unchanged.")
p("- Not recommended: aluminium skin (fire barrier around two diesels, galvanic isolation, not CWF's material); deleting the cover (loses the look); tender-only small-wheel trucks (new design and approval, loses the common spare); lighter rails or holes in rails (coupler load path and fatigue); a smaller generator (hot-humid case is already short).")
p("## 5. Checks to do when detailing")
p("- Skin: 10 ga panels between posts at 500 for wind (C11 pressure) and oil-canning; bolt or plug-weld, no continuous seam welds on the sides.")
p("- Deck: 6 mm tread plate between cross-bearers at ≤ 650 for foot traffic and spill containment; all equipment mounts land on rails or cross-bearers.")
p("- Bolsters: fish-belly web check at the centre plate (≈ 44 kN with ×2 dynamic) and side bearers.")
p("- Genset G1: AWAIT supplier mass, open-frame continuous rating, cooling air and service sides. Fuel 100 L: confirm both engines' real consumption on a run day.")
p("- Truck capacity: at ≈ 7.8–8.1 t the tender puts ≈ 4 t on each truck, below the loaded coach (≈ 6.6 t per truck), so approving the coach truck covers the tender.")
p("## 6. Files")
p("- calcs/tender_weight_study.py → tender_weight_study.json; this memo tender_weight_study.md / .pdf; calc rows C13t/C13u/C13v in calcs.json and PF-CT_R2_calc_notes.")

t2 = json.load(open("/workspace/train/calcs/tender_mass_T2.json"))
p("## 7. Rev T2 — owner-approved subset, now in the model (27 Oct 2026)")
p("- Owner approved S1 (10 ga skin on posts at ≤500, bolted / plug-welded), D1 (6 mm tread-plate deck on 7 C6 cross-bearers), K1 (1.5 mm coal-effect cover) and B1 (fish-belly bolsters). Not adopted: G1 open-skid genset (enclosed genset assumption kept), F1 (150 L fuel kept), L1 (standard 50 mm lining kept).")
p("- Built into build/model.py as tender rev T2 and rebuilt in CAD. The coach / tender Ø600 wheels are now modeled to the true section (≈144 kg each). Deck top is Z1,096 (tread plate on the rail tops; LT45.1 nominal 1,100). Posts come out at 460 pitch on the sides and 498 on the ends (≤500).")
p(f"- Modeled build-up: tender {t2['total_kg']:,} kg (study estimate for this subset {t2['study_estimate_kg']:,} kg; modeled posts and roof bows are heavier than the post allowance, the deck and bolsters are lighter). Saving {t2['saving_kg']:,} kg from {t2['T1_baseline_kg']:,.0f} kg.")
p(f"- 2% start margin at 350 bar: {t2['margin_kN']:.2f} kN (was {t2['margin_T1_kN']:.2f} kN as drawn at rev T1; {t2['margin_ledger_kN']:.2f} kN at the 8,160 kg ledger). {t2['headroom_t']:.2f} t below the ≈{t2['limit_t']:.1f} t limit. Calc row C13u.")
p("| Group | kg |"); p("|---|---|")
for g, v in t2["groups"].items(): p(f"| {g} | {v:,.0f} |")
p(f"| Total | {t2['total_kg']:,} |")

open("/workspace/train/calcs/tender_weight_study.md", "w").write("\n".join(o) + "\n")
